ws in the required CSV format. Recommendation: generate a proper long-form CSV named results_seeded.csv with rows for each seed, each K, each metric (NDCG or Recall). Also compute and export a summary file with mean and std across seeds (Req 6, 7).\n- Aggregation and statistics (Req 6): While per-seed metrics are stored, there is no computation of mean and std across seeds, nor a per-metric table summarizing results. Implement: after all seeds, compute mean and std for each (metric, K) and write a summary file, then log seed-wise comparisons.\n- Reproducibility hygiene (Req 8): Some randomness is controlled, but the implementation uses a custom per-user seed derivation. It would be cleaner to also set Python’s random.seed and ensure all sources of randomness (numpy, Python’s random, LensKit RNG) are explicitly seeded and captured in logs.\n- Edge-case handling (Req 9): Some users might end up with no test items or training items after splitting if thresholds vary. The code currently drops users with fewer than min_interactions in the original data; add explicit checks after split to drop users with zero train or zero test interactions and log these cases.\n- Documentation and configurability (Req 10): The config section is implicit; consider adding a small CLI/config mechanism (argparse or YAML) to set seeds, f, alpha, hyperparameters, and K values, plus a short README-style docstring inside the script explaining experiment design.\n\nConcrete suggestions to raise to fully compliant: \n- Align model config with requirements: instantiate ImplicitMF with n_factors=20, reg=0.01, epochs=15, and ensure deterministic initialization. Replace the per-epoch dummy loop with either a proper training loop or simple evaluation after training.\n- Implement proper results logging: generate and save a CSV at results_seeded.csv with columns [seed, K, metric_name, value], and compute per-metric means and std across seeds in a separate summary file (summary_seeded.csv or similar).\n- 