ets, and the final counts of training/test interactions. This aids interpretation when seeds lead to very different splits.\n- Documentation: Add a short README-style docstring or notes section within the script detailing the experiment plan, seed rationale, and the exact reproducibility guarantees. Also log runtime per seed (start/end timestamps) to a dedicated log file.\n- Reproducibility across environments: If you plan to run across machines or parallel processes, ensure the code uses a deterministic multi-thread setting for any underlying BLAS/NumPy ops and do not rely on non-deterministic multiprocessing by default.\n- Output format extensions: Consider emitting a compact summary (mean and std across seeds) in a human-readable text file (summary_seeded.txt) in addition to summary_seeded.csv, to facilitate quick inspection in reports.\n\nOverall, the current design largely fulfills the required components for the seed-experiment with a few caveats around strict ImplicitMF usage and output robustness. Addressing the notes above will lift the implementation toward a fully reproducible, production-grade experiment.', is_satisfactory=True)
